# kind | name | source (on-disk LICENSE path for shards; SPDX id for clib/runtime)
#
# Only what the released binary actually embeds: ameba and spectator are
# development dependencies and never end up in it. Add a `shard` line here for
# every runtime dependency added to shard.yml — nothing checks that for you,
# and a missing notice in a redistributed static binary is precisely the fault
# this file exists to prevent.
#
# The clib list is the set Alpine installs in the build stage of the Dockerfile,
# deliberately erring on the side of listing one library too many: an extra
# notice costs nothing, a missing one does not. This binary links zlib, pcre2,
# boehm-gc and musl, plus openssl, which HTTP::Client requires for TLS
# (src/http/client.cr of the stdlib); the rest appear as soon as the code
# requires yaml, xml, big or compress from the stdlib, which is exactly why
# they are listed up front rather than added after the fact.
#
# CONFIRMED, not assumed. Each SPDX id below was checked on 2026-08-09 against
# the `L:` field apk records in the build image itself, and the link line was
# captured from `crystal build --static --verbose` inside that image:
#   template  -lz -lpcre2-8 -lgc -lpthread -ldl
#   + stdlib  -lgmp -lxml2 -lm -llzma -lyaml -lssl -lcrypto
# Versions as of that check: openssl 3.5.7, pcre2 10.47, yaml 0.2.5,
# libxml2 2.13.9, zlib 1.3.2, xz 5.8.3, gc 8.2.12, musl 1.2.6, gcc 15.2.0,
# gmp 6.3.0, crystal 1.20.3. Re-run the check when the Alpine base moves.
#
# TWO ENTRIES CARRY A JUDGEMENT, recorded here so nobody has to re-derive it:
#   liblzma — apk labels the whole xz suite "GPL-2.0-or-later AND 0BSD AND
#     Public-Domain AND LGPL-2.1-or-later", but the GPL parts are the
#     command-line tools. The binary links liblzma alone, which is 0BSD.
#   gmp — dual licensed "LGPL-3.0-or-later OR GPL-2.0-or-later"; the LGPL arm is
#     the one relied on, since the GPL arm would reach the whole program.
#     BEWARE: LGPLv3 §4 asks more of a STATIC link than a notice — the recipient
#     must be able to relink against a modified GMP. Shipping the object files
#     or a dynamically linked build is a product decision, not a build detail.
shard   | baked_file_system | lib/baked_file_system/LICENSE
shard   | watch             | lib/watch/LICENSE
clib    | openssl           | Apache-2.0
clib    | pcre2             | BSD-3-Clause
clib    | libyaml           | MIT
clib    | libxml2           | MIT
clib    | zlib              | Zlib
clib    | liblzma           | 0BSD
clib    | gmp               | LGPL-3.0-or-later
clib    | boehm-gc          | Boehm-GC
clib    | musl              | MIT
clib    | libgcc            | GCC-runtime-exception
runtime | crystal           | Apache-2.0
project | icinga-pagerduty  | LICENSE
